hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2728","Narrated to us Nasr ibn Marzuq al-Misri: narrated to us Asad — meaning Ibn Musa al-Sunna: narrated to us Sa'id ibn Zayd: narrated to us 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib: narrated to us Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said:\nIbn 'Abbas (RA) would say, “Preserve this hadith,” and he would raise it to the Prophet (ﷺ). He would supplicate with it between the two corners (of the Ka'bah):\n“O Allah, grant me contentment with what You have provided me, bless me in it, and replace for me every absent thing with good.”\n\nCHAPTER:"
